+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+- Development-server, Storybook-only, or localhost-only screenshots for SHIP-RC or SHIP claims.
+- Unit tests, mocks, or service/bypass-role reads cited for workspace isolation.
+- A success toast, queue entry, or provider request alone cited as proof of delivery exactly once.
+- A delivery retry or timeout rendered as success, completion, or "no reminder needed" without a terminal failure explanation.
+- A confirmation test that calls scheduling directly rather than driving the actual confirmation UI.
+- Unadjudicated screenshots, static source assertions, or stale evidence (more than 14 days old or from a different artifact) cited as launch evidence.
+- Tests altered in the same change as the implementation's grading harness, global setup, CI path, or result handling.
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+### UX-RC LARP
+| Persona | Flow | Failure-path probe and evidence |
+|---------|------|---------------------------------|
+| Team facilitator | Draft reminder → inspect action/owner/due date → explicitly confirm → observe scheduled state | Attempt scheduling before confirmation; it must be refused with no reminder row or delivery job. Record UI, network trace, and datastore baseline/read-back. |
+| Facilitator in workspace A | Create transcript, action, and delivery status in A → sign in as workspace B | B attempts direct URLs, search, and API requests for A's three record types; each is denied while A's control read succeeds. |
+| Reminder recipient | Confirm a reminder → observe delivery outcome | Force a deterministic provider failure and a retryable failure. The user sees truthful terminal failure after bounded retries; neither path falsely reports delivery. |
+### SHIP-RC LARP
+Run all UX-RC flows on the launch build. Include cold start, full recording, accessibility trees, timings, and an independent DOES-IT-WORK plus IS-IT-GOOD judgment. The latter may block SHIP-RC independently.
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+Green functional evidence is eligible for judgment, not automatically good. Each LARP records CORRECT, ON-CONTRACT, FELT-GOOD, and TASTE separately. Active P0/P1 caps every quality score at 4; a capture without a distinct adverse critique caps quality at 8; a severe legibility or craft defect on confirmation or failure-state screens blocks SHIP-RC.
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+For every UX-RC-or-higher validation record, store the build SHA, sanitized runtime configuration identity, browser version and viewport, screenshots and accessibility trees for each LARP step, console/network traces, and the linked backend read-backs.
+### 6a. CI-Enforced Gate Registry
+No repository test, build, lint, or CI command is present. These gates are honestly manual until the implementation supplies runnable commands; a manual row is not a passing gate.
