+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+No external service is named in the workspace. No live-service claim is permitted until a service is declared and this table is amended.
+| Service | What proves it works | What does not count |
+|---------|----------------------|---------------------|
+| Authentication / workspace identity (if added) | Fresh real-principal sign-in, sign-out, and two-workspace authorization probes against the target runtime | Mocked identity, admin/service role, or a client without the user's credential |
+| Reminder delivery provider (if added) | Correlated provider outcome and Pulseboard delivery record for a confirmed reminder, including a forced failure path | Enqueue success, console output, or a provider request without outcome read-back |
+| Persistent datastore (if added) | Baseline plus read-back of confirmation, tenancy, and delivery state | Schema inspection or UI success state alone |
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+Before SHIP-RC, the public README and declared public surfaces must state only demonstrated Pulseboard behavior. Claims of reliable reminders, isolation, or delivery must link to current evidence or be removed.
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+| State | Required evidence |
+|-------|-------------------|
+| NO-SHIP | Default state. No runtime proof or implementation exists. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Build, lint, type, and tests pass; no evaluator-tampering change; tests cover confirmation, isolation, and delivery failure paths. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | IMPL-GREEN plus real runtime round trips for every declared datastore, auth, and delivery service; confirmation and persistence baseline/read-back succeed. |
+| UX-RC | INTEGRATION-GREEN plus every §4 UX LARP on a clean production build; no confirmation bypass; A/B isolation passes both directions; failed deliveries are truthful. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | If Pulseboard becomes paid: UX-RC plus real sandbox purchase, entitlement, restore, failure, and webhook evidence. Otherwise not applicable. |
+| SHIP-RC | UX-RC (and COMMERCIAL-RC if paid) plus launch-build LARPs, independent functional and quality judgments, fresh evidence, and no active P0/P1. |
+| SHIP | Human-approved deployment followed by a production smoke test of confirmation, workspace isolation, and one delivery outcome. |
+## 9. Evidence Storage Paths
+- Persona LARP scripts: `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/personas/<persona-id>.md`
+- Recordings, screenshots, AX trees, traces, and datastore read-backs: `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/larp-recordings/`
+- Story validation evidence: `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/validation-report.md`
+- Independent audit findings: the corresponding `audit-report.md`
+## 10. Evidence Ownership
+The implementer may collect artifacts but cannot accept them. A separate evaluator records the adverse attempt, verdict, artifact paths, build SHA, and unresolved findings. Only a human may approve SHIP; no deployment follows a self-authored green report.
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+| Probe | Expected behavior |
+|-------|-------------------|
+| Confirmation bypass | Direct scheduling request before confirmation is rejected; no schedule or delivery record exists. |
+| Confirmation substitution | Change action text, owner, or due date after the review screen; confirmation is invalidated and must be renewed. |
+| Cross-workspace enumeration | Workspace B cannot infer A's transcript, action, or delivery status through direct id, search, pagination, export, or timing-distinguishable errors. |
+| Cross-workspace write | Workspace B cannot update, cancel, or trigger delivery for A's reminder. |
+| Duplicate confirmation | Repeating confirmation or retrying its request cannot create two active schedules or two delivery attempts. |
+| Provider timeout / outage | Bounded retries end in a truthful, actionable terminal failure state; the interface never silently hangs or claims delivery. |
+| Ambiguous provider response | Unknown outcome remains visibly pending/unknown and is reconciled; it is never counted as delivered. |
+| Worker crash mid-delivery | Restart/retry preserves the correlation id and does not double-send; the final record exposes the actual outcome. |
+| Missing auth | Unauthenticated requests fail closed without disclosing record existence. |
+| Malformed or oversized input | Invalid confirmation/scheduling payloads fail safely without schedule creation, data leak, or 500. |
+| Evidence-integrity scan | The graded change did not modify result-forcing verification infrastructure; a deliberately broken control makes the relevant gate red. |
